    {
      "id": "claim_450fc9577c344cffafbf86f9739b38c9",
      "statement": "The practical rule for cross-domain changes: if a change touches more than one domain, update the shared protocol or ADR first, then the relay/server, then the browser adapters. For a protocol or browser-capability change cutting across layers, check the full path: shared protocol -> WebSocket relay -> MCP surface -> shared controller -> Chrome adapter -> Safari adapter -> integration tests. This matches the AGENTS.md ownership rule and keeps the repo's explicit-contract style intact.",
      "evidence": [
